  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ARC Strengthening Community Preparedness and Response to Epidemics in the Pacific (Asia-Pacific)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program strengthens community engagement to support communicable disease prevention and preparedness, including community-based surveillance; delivering enhanced data for decision making; conducting community-led vector control, vaccine communication and outbreak response; and enhancing the One Health approach at the primary health level in Fiji and Vanuatu. The program goal is to strengthen community capacity in Fiji and Vanuatu to play a pivotal role in building resilient and equitable health systems to anticipate, prevent, detect and respond effectively to communicable disease threats.</narrative>
  </description>
